- [[strategies/QM5_1305-camarilla-vwap-confluence-intraday]] — Camarilla-pivot fade with VWAP-bias filter. Same fade-direction edge (mean-reversion intraday), but the trigger is a fixed-pivot level (Camarilla) not a dynamic-σ-band. P2 will show whether the σ-band trigger or the pivot trigger is cleaner.
- [[strategies/QM5_1294-williams-r-ema200-mr-h1]] — Williams%R mean-reversion on H1 with EMA200 bias. Same family (overbought-fade with macro-bias-consistency) but H1 rolling-window (vs M15 session-anchored). Different temporal scale.
- [[strategies/QM5_1290-classic-pivot-points-fade-break]] — classic-pivot fade is a *fixed-level* fade (one set of levels per day); QM5_1320 is a *continuously-evolving* statistical fade band. Different level construction.

